1
00:00:03,866 --> 00:00:08,601
Whiskers and Luna's World. Episode nine. Weather and Seasons!

2
00:00:15,083 --> 00:00:18,748
One windy morning, the leaves were falling outside.

3
00:00:18,948 --> 00:00:22,596
Luna! The tree is losing its leaves! Is it broken?

4
00:00:22,796 --> 00:00:26,115
Not broken, silly. It's autumn! The seasons are changing.

5
00:00:29,215 --> 00:00:32,585
Can we skip to summer? I miss my sunny nap spot.

6
00:00:32,785 --> 00:00:34,538
Why do we even have seasons?

7
00:00:34,738 --> 00:00:37,019
Let's ask a weather expert. Hold on!

8
00:00:45,435 --> 00:00:47,025
Up, up they flew!

9
00:00:53,024 --> 00:00:56,939
Here's our home, in Europe. And nearby lives a very famous rooster!

10
00:01:07,771 --> 00:01:11,236
On a red barn stood a shiny weather-vane rooster.

11
00:01:14,819 --> 00:01:19,406
Cock-a-doodle-doo! Behold, Sir Rufus! The finest rooster in the world!

12
00:01:19,606 --> 00:01:23,162
Whoa! The wind spins me round! Wind is moving air.

13
00:01:27,711 --> 00:01:30,180
Whoa! I can't see the air, but I can feel it!

14
00:01:30,380 --> 00:01:33,018
Excuse me! Coming through! Acorns for winter!

15
00:01:33,218 --> 00:01:37,275
Ah, Hazel! She knows the seasons best. After me, of course.

16
00:01:37,475 --> 00:01:40,029
Watch my tree! In spring, it grows flowers.

17
00:01:43,612 --> 00:01:46,163
Summer is warm and sunny, with long days.

18
00:01:49,746 --> 00:01:52,139
In autumn, the leaves turn orange, and fall.

19
00:01:55,722 --> 00:01:58,846
In winter, the water in the clouds freezes. Snow!

20
00:02:02,912 --> 00:02:05,813
Spring, summer, autumn, winter. Then round again!

21
00:02:09,879 --> 00:02:12,364
Is summer when the Earth gets closer to the Sun?

22
00:02:12,564 --> 00:02:15,632
A common mistake! To space, my friends!

23
00:02:23,564 --> 00:02:26,671
In space, the Earth travels around the Sun.

24
00:02:26,871 --> 00:02:32,389
One trip takes a year. And look! The Earth is tilted. It always leans the same way!

25
00:02:46,604 --> 00:02:51,186
Our half leans toward the Sun: strong sunshine, long days. Summer!

26
00:02:54,769 --> 00:02:58,426
Leaning away: weak sunshine, short days. Winter!

27
00:03:02,009 --> 00:03:04,451
So it's not because the Earth gets closer?

28
00:03:04,651 --> 00:03:08,336
No! The distance stays about the same. It's the tilt!

29
00:03:12,402 --> 00:03:15,717
And when Europe leans toward the Sun, Australia leans away.

30
00:03:19,300 --> 00:03:22,780
So, summer in Europe is winter in Australia!

31
00:03:22,980 --> 00:03:26,829
Then I'll nap in Australia every winter. Summer forever!

32
00:03:38,144 --> 00:03:41,764
Rain! It falls from clouds, just like Drip in the water cycle.

33
00:03:45,347 --> 00:03:48,926
Aha! Sun and rain together. Rainbow weather!

34
00:03:49,126 --> 00:03:52,604
A rainbow? I'll look right at the sun. Sunglasses on!

35
00:03:58,120 --> 00:04:01,130
No rainbow. Just sun. Lots of sun.

36
00:04:01,330 --> 00:04:04,322
Turn around! The sun must be behind you.

37
00:04:10,321 --> 00:04:14,268
I knew that. I looked at the sun on purpose. For my suntan.

38
00:04:19,301 --> 00:04:21,583
Ooh! A flash of lightning, far away!

39
00:04:21,783 --> 00:04:24,448
Let's count. One... two... three...

40
00:04:28,031 --> 00:04:31,227
Thunder! Light is faster than sound, so the flash comes first.

41
00:04:31,427 --> 00:04:34,260
It's far away. Farewell, my friends!

42
00:04:40,259 --> 00:04:45,283
Remember! One. There are four seasons: spring, summer, autumn and winter.

43
00:04:47,658 --> 00:04:51,167
Two. We have seasons because the Earth is tilted.

44
00:04:53,542 --> 00:04:56,876
Three. A rainbow needs sun and rain together.

45
00:05:02,391 --> 00:05:08,128
Quiz time! Why do we have seasons? Is the Earth closer to the Sun, or is it tilted?

46
00:05:11,107 --> 00:05:14,038
Because the Earth is tilted! Well done!

47
00:05:16,172 --> 00:05:20,530
Next. What makes a rainbow? Snow and wind, or sun and rain?

48
00:05:23,509 --> 00:05:25,676
Sun and rain, together!

49
00:05:31,676 --> 00:05:34,390
And with a twinkle, they were home again.

50
00:05:34,590 --> 00:05:36,708
Look! Luna's globe is tilted too!

51
00:05:39,324 --> 00:05:42,799
Autumn's not so bad. Perfect for a cosy nap.

52
00:05:45,899 --> 00:05:48,518
Next time, day and night! Goodnight!

